- action(n4, "You have completed this procedure"): Hallucinates a final confirmation step; the source explicitly terminates the workflow immediately after the cutting action ("Once the banana has been cut, the process will come to an end.").
- action(n1, "start the process to cut the banana"): Payload misrepresents the source directive "prepare yourself to cut the banana," replacing a specific preparatory behavior with a generic meta-process label.